      "explanation": "<p>Gabriel phthalimide synthesis is used to prepare 1<sup>o</sup> aliphatic or alicyclic amine. Hence, amine which can be synthesised by Gabriel phthalimide synthesis method contains <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-carbon.</p>\n<p>Aniline (C<sub>6</sub>H<sub>5</sub>NH<sub>2</sub>) does not contain <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-C cannot be prepared by Gabriel reaction.</p>\n<p>Remaining amines all contain <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-C in its respective position, hence they can easily give Gabriel phthalimide reaction.</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3qujhs5/3f5bcf89-b9fb-40be-ab20-0bceb73bb92c/14f6af50-df0e-11ec-86f8-635a8b4f9122/file-1l3qujhs6.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3qujhs5/3f5bcf89-b9fb-40be-ab20-0bceb73bb92c/14f6af50-df0e-11ec-86f8-635a8b4f9122/file-1l3qujhs6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 24th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 184 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3qujhs5/3f5bcf89-b9fb-40be-ab20-0bceb73bb92c/14f6af50-df0e-11ec-86f8-635a8b4f9122/file-1l3qujhs6.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3qujhs5/3f5bcf89-b9fb-40be-ab20-0bceb73bb92c/14f6af50-df0e-11ec-86f8-635a8b4f9122/file-1l3qujhs6.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3qujhs5/3f5bcf89-b9fb-40be-ab20-0bceb73bb92c/14f6af50-df0e-11ec-86f8-635a8b4f9122/file-1l3qujhs6.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3qujhs5/3f5bcf89-b9fb-40be-ab20-0bceb73bb92c/14f6af50-df0e-11ec-86f8-635a8b4f9122/file-1l3qujhs6.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3qujhs5/3f5bcf89-b9fb-40be-ab20-0bceb73bb92c/14f6af50-df0e-11ec-86f8-635a8b4f9122/file-1l3qujhs6.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3qujhs5/3f5bcf89-b9fb-40be-ab20-0bceb73bb92c/14f6af50-df0e-11ec-86f8-635a8b4f9122/file-1l3qujhs6.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">"
